# Build-context filter for Dockerfile.edge-prebuilt only.
#
# BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore` from the Dockerfile's own
# directory in preference to the repository-root .dockerignore. The root file
# excludes every `dist` directory so that a stale build output can never land
# in the source-built images (Dockerfile.edge rebuilds the frontend itself;
# base-rust-warm and g5d-g5dev COPY the whole tree). This image is the one
# consumer of a prebuilt frontend/dist (written by the CI `frontend-build` step
# and by the self-hosted install workflow), so admit exactly the paths its COPY
# lines read and nothing else. Keep this list in step with the COPY lines in
# Dockerfile.edge-prebuilt; scripts/test_edge_prebuilt_dockerignore.py checks it.
*
!frontend/dist
!infra/docker/Caddyfile
!infra/docker/caddy-ci-tls.caddyfile
!infra/docker/edge-entrypoint.sh
